# Agent Doctrine & Execution Plan (Farfalle ↔ CRM)

## Purpose
Define exactly what we will build, where code lives, how pieces integrate, and the step‑by‑step plan to ship end‑to‑end intelligence for a Lead/Organization using Farfalle (chat/orchestrator) and CRM (APIs/UI).

## Canonical References (read these first)
- Specialist agent patterns: [specialist_agent_patterns.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/specialist_agent_patterns.mdc)
- Intelligence system overview (what we aimed to achieve): [INTELLIGENCE_SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md](mdc:crm-deployment/scripts/docs/INTELLIGENCE_SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md)
- Legacy monolith (for lessons learned, not to reuse directly): [dynamic_crm_intelligence_system.py](mdc:crm-deployment/scripts/dynamic_crm_intelligence_system.py)
- Farfalle code (current, real path): `crm-deployment/scripts/farfalle-main/`
  - FastAPI app entry: `src/backend/main.py`
  - Chat flow: `src/backend/chat.py`
  - Semantic intel module: `src/backend/intel/{router.py, services.py}`
  - Search providers: `src/backend/search/providers/`
  - CRM adapter location (moved): `crm-deployment/scripts/farfalle-main/crm/{client.py, tools.py}`

## What we will ship (initial scope)
- Use case: “Analyze this lead/company” → Farfalle performs web search enrichment (Tavily + optional providers), synthesizes results, and returns a concise summary + sources; optionally push a Note/Attachment into CRM.
- UI surfaces:
  - Desk/SPA page `/crm/ai` (exists) to trigger analysis and view results
  - Optional: Human Inbox/Notes linkage for saving outputs
- Backends:
  - Farfalle exposes/intakes: `POST /intel/analyze` (already present) and a thin `POST /intel/enrich_lead` that accepts `{company, domain?}` and forwards to the service
  - CRM remains the system of record; Farfalle uses CRM APIs via adapters if saving notes/tasks

## Architecture (folders)
- Farfalle (copilot): `crm-deployment/scripts/farfalle-main/`
  - `src/backend/main.py` → include intel router + new enrich endpoint
  - `src/backend/intel/services.py` → IntelligenceService (Tavily/Diffbot/LinkedIn)
  - `crm/{client.py, tools.py}` → CRM session/CSRF + helper tool calls
- CRM (Frappe app): `crm-deployment/crm/` (no changes needed for intel read-only path; save notes via existing endpoints if desired)
- SPA: `frappe-bench/apps/crm/frontend/` (`src/pages/AiCopilot.vue` calls Farfalle)

## Step‑by‑Step Plan
1) Audit & wire Farfalle intel
   - Verify `src/backend/intel/router.py` is included in `main.py`
   - Add `POST /intel/enrich_lead` in `src/backend/intel/router.py` (or a small new router) that:
     - Validates body `{ company: str, domain?: str }`
     - Calls `IntelligenceService.analyze(company, default_questions, domain)`
     - Returns summary + sources (contract below)
2) SPA integration
   - Extend `src/pages/AiCopilot.vue` to submit `{company, domain}` to Farfalle `/intel/enrich_lead`
   - Render summary bullets and top sources; add links
3) Optional: persist results to CRM
   - Use `crm/tools.py` to call a Note insert or attach a JSON artifact to the Lead/Organization
   - Gate with a “Save to CRM” button
4) Observability & guardrails
   - Structured logs for intel calls (latency, provider usage)
   - 429/5xx retry/backoff; timeouts
   - Env configuration via `.env-template` (keys: TAVILY_API_KEY, DIFFBOT_TOKEN, LINKEDIN_RAPIDAPI_KEY)

## Endpoint Contracts
- Farfalle `POST /intel/enrich_lead`
  - Request:
    ```json
    { "company": "Abbey Capital", "domain": "abbeycapital.com" }
    ```
  - Response:
    ```json
    {
      "company": "Abbey Capital",
      "summary": ["3-6 bullet points"],
      "results": [
        { "question": "Who are the decision-makers?", "answer": "…", "sources": [{"title":"…","url":"…"}], "extracted_people": [{"name":"…","title":"…"}] },
        { "question": "Recent investments?", "answer": "…", "sources": [ … ] }
      ],
      "total_sources": 9
    }
    ```
- SPA consumes this and renders; optional “Save to CRM” invokes CRM adapter to create a Note

## Tests & Demos
- Local Farfalle:
  - `poetry install && poetry run uvicorn backend.main:app --reload --port 8000`
  - `curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/intel/enrich_lead -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"company":"Abbey Capital","domain":"abbeycapital.com"}'`
- SPA:
  - Open `/crm/ai`, analyze known companies; verify summary & links
- (Optional) Save to CRM:
  - Click “Save to CRM”; confirm Note or Attachment on the Lead/Organization

## Out‑of‑scope (for now)
- The legacy monolith [dynamic_crm_intelligence_system.py](mdc:crm-deployment/scripts/dynamic_crm_intelligence_system.py); we will reuse ideas only
- Full agentic specialist network; we will start with single intel path (Tavily-first)
- Heavy provider orchestration (async/rate limiting/caching) beyond minimal retries

## Risks & Mitigations
- Provider failures → fail-soft, partial results; retry/backoff
- Missing domain → still run Tavily on company name; ask user for domain if needed
- CSRF/auth to CRM → adapters already manage session+token; only used if saving output

## Iteration Notes
We will keep pruning/expanding this plan as we implement. Next iteration will add: routing from chat intent to intel (keyword router), and an option to generate a CRM Note automatically.